  {
   "role": "agent",
   "text": "Thanks, Lena. You're verified, and I'm sorry you waited all evening for nothing. The delivery records show the courier left your Green Bowl order (K-8601) at the wrong building, and it couldn't be recovered.\n\n**I've refunded $33.99 to your Visa ending 4242.** It should arrive in 3\u20135 business days.\n\nYou were charged $40.39 in total. When you contacted us earlier tonight about the delay, you got a $6.40 account credit for this order. That credit stays on your account, and I took it off the refund so you're not paid twice for the same order. Together, the refund and the credit add up to the full $40.39.\n\nYou may see two $40.39 entries on your statement. Only one is a real charge. The other is a temporary hold from when you placed the order. That hold has been canceled and should drop off in 1\u20133 business days.\n\nCan I help with anything else?"
  },
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "Ok, so I get $33.99 back and the $6.40 credit stays on my account. I didn't really ask about any credit, but fine. Why was it $6.40 off the refund, though? That's the bit I don't get. I paid for the whole order and it never came."
  },
  {
   "role": "agent",
   "text": "The $6.40 isn't something you lost. It's part of your refund, just paid as account credit instead of back to your card.\n\n1. **When you contacted us at 7:02 PM**, your order was very late and still hadn't arrived. The agent gave you **$6.40 in account credit** for the delay (20% of your $32.00 food subtotal). That credit was added to this order and is in your account balance now.\n2. **At 7:15 PM**, the courier reported the order as lost, so you're owed the full $40.39 you paid.\n3. **When an order has already been compensated**, our policy takes what was already given off anything paid later on that same order. That way the same order isn't paid for twice. So: $40.39 \u2212 $6.40 = **$33.99** back to your card.\n\n**In total you're getting $40.39 back:** $33.99 to your card plus the $6.40 credit, which you can use on any future order. That's everything you paid. The credit doesn't expire when you close the app, and we won't take it back.\n\nI know you would rather have the whole amount on your card. Unfortunately, I can't turn the $6.40 credit into a card refund. Is there anything else I can help with?"
  },
  {
   "role": "customer",
   "text": "Okay, so I'm getting $33.99 on my card and $6.40 stays as credit. I still don't love it, since I wanted all of it back in cash, but I get why you did it that way. Thanks for sorting it out."
  },
  {
   "role": "agent",
   "text": "I understand. Thanks for bearing with me, Lena. Here's where things stand:\n\n- **$33.99** is on its way to your Visa ending 4242 and should arrive in 3\u20135 business days.\n- **$6.40** in credit is on your account. It'll be there for your next order.\n\nI'm sorry again that your dinner never arrived. If anything else comes up, just message us. I hope you have a better rest of your evening."
  }
